{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And if the Jubilee comes, etc., their inheritance shall be diminished.</b> And even though the entire land has not yet been conquered — as it says (Exodus 23:30), ״מְעַט מְעַט אֲגָרְשֶׁנּוּ מִפָּנֶיךָ״ — and each tribe needs to conquer its own portion, nevertheless even if some individual sells his portion to another from a different tribe, the seller will not on this account refrain from exerting himself with his tribe to conquer, for it will return to him in the Jubilee. But the portion of the daughters, which does not revert in the Jubilee — the men of the tribe will not exert themselves to conquer it, or they will leave inhabitants of the land there since it belongs to another tribe, and thus the conquered territory of their inheritance will be diminished from the lot of the tribal fathers."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:41:42.756695552Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}